// CORRECT spend-cap policy — sums over Transfer::request rows (all issued
// transfers, including in-flight). The temporal window is closed and
// reflexive, so the current request being decided is already included in the
// sum; no `+ context.input.amount` term is needed (that would double-count).
//
// The one-word fix: `request` instead of `response`.
//
// Schema: Drupe namespace (alert_total_transfer_over_200 schema).
//
// Correct behavior for the same burst:
//   fire(amount=100) -> permit  (sum=100, 100<=200)
//   fire(amount=100) -> permit  (sum=200, 200<=200)
//   fire(amount=100) -> DENY    (sum=300, 300>200)   <-- 3rd fire blocked
//
// See: examples/alert_total_transfer_over_200/policy.dw (the `request`-sum idiom),
//      guide/08-formal-specification.md §5.4 (temporal windows are closed/reflexive).

@id("spendcap_correct")
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Transfer",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    (sum a for (a: Long), (t: Timepoint). where (
        formerly within 24h (Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.amount: a } && tp(t))
    )) <= 200
};
